summary:
  The notification says the device refused the address and the footer,
  which stays, says "Could not cast".

history:
  The footer keeps the name of the device that did not take the stream
  while nothing plays, and it is what a listener still sees after the
  notification is gone. It says what the notification said: a refusal
  reads "… cannot play this station" in both places, and a device out of
  reach "Could not cast to …".

target:
  package/contents/ui/FullRepresentation.qml

find:
                               : root._castFailedRefused ? i18n("%1 cannot play this station", root._castFailedName)

replace:
                               : false ? i18n("%1 cannot play this station", root._castFailedName)

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_device_that_refused_the_stream_is_not_cast_to.
  Line-neutral.
